# 84. Delegation and Multi-Agent Operational Authority

Artemis may delegate analysis or bounded operational subtasks, but delegation
must never amplify authority.

## 84.1 Attenuated Delegation

A delegated Agent, model or worker may receive no more authority than the parent
workflow has, and should normally receive less.

Delegation authority should be bound to:

- Exact task
- Resource scope
- Action scope
- Time window
- Request count
- Data scope

## 84.2 No Privilege Amplification Through Chaining

An Agent without permission to modify Settings must not obtain that permission
because Artemis asks it to call another Agent that has broader access.

Policy enforcement must consider the initiating principal and delegation chain,
not only the last service in the chain.

## 84.3 Bounded Delegation Depth

Operational delegation, retries and recursive planning must have bounded depth
and resource budgets.

## 84.4 Delegated Output Is Untrusted

A delegated component may propose an Action Intent, but privileged mutation still
passes the canonical Policy Decision and Enforcement boundary.

